  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 234 AM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge builds in late Thursday, remaining \nin place through Friday, keeping highs Friday warm into the 60s. The \nnext system moves in Friday evening as a cold front. This cold front \nwill bring cooler air behind it, unlike the one earlier in the week, \nbringing cooler than normal temperatures into the upper 30s to 40s. \nPrecipitation chances will remain limited, generally just across far \nnorth central Nebraska, although lower probabilities, less than 30 \npercent chance of 0.05 qpf of rainfall, with even lower probabilities,\ngenerally under 20 percent, for qpf values at 0.10 or greater, \nleading to greater confidence in precipitation not occurring. \n\nCooler temperatures continue for the weekend into early \nnext week with quasi zonal flow continuing through Monday. A trof \nmoves through Tuesday, there will be a slight chance for \nprecipitation Tuesday afternoon/evening. Will need to monitor this \nsystem, as temperatures will be quite cool with highs only in the \nupper 30s, thus any precipitation that occurs later in the evening \nmay have the potential to be a rain/snow mix.",
